WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.319
Film Courage: How do you think making WALLY
GOT WASTED helped you to move forward?

00:00:04.319 --> 00:00:08.920
Adam William Ward, Actor/Producer: WALLY GOT
WASTED is my first feature so to be moving

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.940
forward after it?

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.610
How does it help me move forward?

00:00:12.610 --> 00:00:20.430
It’s kind of amazing and I try to explain
this to people but until you’ve done a feature

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:24.570
people don’t believe you can do a feature
because so many people have failed at doing

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:30.369
a feature so just a lot more doors open up
in a way.

00:00:30.369 --> 00:00:34.930
People know that you’ve done it and if it’s
at least half decent they think you can do

00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.180
it again.

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:43.311
Actually I think I read something that 99%
of filmmakers make their first feature, they

00:00:43.311 --> 00:00:45.120
never make a feature again.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.442
So that’s how many people try to do this
and go “I don’t want to do this again.

00:00:48.442 --> 00:00:49.980
This is horrible.”

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:55.420
You have to really love film to want to do
it because it’s so hard.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:01:00.740
Like I said earlier it’s like 2-3 hours
a night I slept on WALLY and how many emergencies

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.920
would happen or whatever and everything comes
back on me so if you don’t like to be a

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.580
leader you are not going to like being a film
director.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.890
You have to manage egos.

00:01:09.890 --> 00:01:17.820
You have to manage…you have to keep your
cool under all circumstances and at the same

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:19.210
time make decisions.

00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:22.210
You don’t want to put anybody in danger.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:25.500
Your movie is important but you are making
a movie we are not curing cancer.

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:30.340
So let’s not endanger anybody or do anything
that is unsafe.

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:34.340
After you’ve done your first feature it’s
just a totally different respect you get from

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:40.470
people and opportunities open up way more
because now you are a real filmmaker.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:44.070
I mean everybody kind of looks at you like
an amateur when you are making short films.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.810
But after you’ve made a feature you are
in the pros.

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:52.659
You are competing with…once you make a feature
you are competing with AVENGERS.

00:01:52.659 --> 00:01:54.650
You are competing with all of the movies.

00:01:54.650 --> 00:01:58.870
There is no scale because you are competing
with them all.

00:01:58.870 --> 00:02:04.729
Because the audience on Amazon can choose
AVENGERS or they can choose WALLY GOT WASTED.

00:02:04.729 --> 00:02:10.170
So you are competing with everybody so that’s
why I take it easy on myself because I didn’t

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:16.130
have 500 million dollars to make a movie,
I had 70,000.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:20.800
The fact that I’m even competing with these
movies and some people are watching my movie,

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.800
I’m thrilled.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:29.470
Because there is so much content out there
to watch but you learn and opportunities just

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.470
open up.

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:32.950
They open up and you don’t know where they
are going to come from after you’ve done

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.410
your first feature so you’ve just got to
do it.

00:02:35.410 --> 00:02:36.920
You’ve got to take your first chance.

00:02:36.920 --> 00:02:40.840
You’ve got to learn and you’ve got to
fall on your face and you’ve got to do it.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.650
Even if it never sees the light of day at
least you did it and you can do it again.

